    Six actuators drive twelve revolute joints through fixed tendons.  The
    passive springs open the hand and select its free-space posture, while the
    unconstrained joints redistribute tendon travel after contact.  This is a
    deliberately compliant underactuated model; no equality loop is used.
  -->
